course: dictionary
lesson: 14776
title: Provisions and provision
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words look alike but have more than one meaning. Provisions, with an s, usually means supplies of food and drink that people take on a journey. Provision, without an s, means providing something people need. Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
explain: «The explorers packed tents, warm clothes and provisions for six months.» Packed and explorers are the clues. A long journey needs food and drink, so provisions means supplies of food. Try your meaning in the sentence: «packed tents, warm clothes and food» still makes sense.
explain: «The town council made provision for a new school.» Here provision means planning and arranging for something people need. Made provision for is a phrase that means arranged for or prepared for. The word for and the rest of the sentence show you the meaning.
fact: Provisions (plural) means supplies of food and drink, especially for a journey.
fact: Provision (no s) means the act of providing something people need, such as «provision of clean water».
fact: Provision can also mean a part of a law or agreement that says what must happen. This is a formal use.
fact: «Run out of provisions» means having no food or drink left. «Make provision for» means prepare or arrange for something.
fact: A good check is to swap in a simple word like food or supplies and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The sailors checked their provisions before they set sail.» What are provisions here? | Friendly people on the shore | Maps of the sea | *Supplies of food and drink | Sails and ropes
exercise: «The hospital's provision of clean water saved many lives.» What does provision mean here? | A part of a law | Stopping something from happening | Buying a new boat | *The act of supplying something people need
exercise: «The expedition ran out of provisions in the snow.» What does ran out of provisions mean? | Sent a letter home | Found a shop with a sale | Had lots of food to spare | *Had no food or drink left
test: «The council made provision for a new park.» What does made provision for mean? | Forgot about it completely | Sold the land to a builder | *Arranged for something people will need | Argued against it
test: In the phrase «the provision of schools», what does provision mean? | *The act of providing schools | A school bell | A bag of food for a trip | Closing a school for good
exam: Ahmed says, «We have provisions for five days.» What does provisions mean? | Spare clothes for a camping trip | *Supplies of food and drink | Rules that a camp must follow | Nights spent sleeping outside
